course: dictionary
lesson: 2487
title: Learning a word from its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A deadline is the latest time or day by which something must be done or handed in. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «The project deadline is Friday.» The word project and the day Friday tell you a deadline is the last time to hand something in.
explain: Look at how people use it. You can «meet» a deadline, which means you finish in time, or «miss» a deadline, which means you finish too late. «A tight deadline» means there is very little time left to do the job.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «I finished my homework before the deadline» still makes sense if deadline means the last time to finish, so your meaning fits.
fact: A deadline is the latest time or day by which something must be done or handed in.
fact: «Meet a deadline» means finish in time; «miss a deadline» means finish too late.
fact: «A tight deadline» means there is very little time to do the job.
fact: «Extend the deadline» means move it to a later time.
fact: Work back from a deadline: for a 10:15 flight, being at the airport 2 hours early means you must arrive at 8:15.
fact: Old use: a deadline was once a line in a prison that prisoners must not cross.
exercise: «The project deadline is Friday.» What is a deadline? | The first day of the project | *The latest time by which something must be done | A game played by a team | A kind of prize
exercise: «Our team has a tight deadline.» What does tight mean here? | Very cold | *Very little time is left | Very loose and easy | A bright colour
exercise: Ellie's flight leaves at 10:15 and she must be at the airport 2 hours early. What time must she arrive? | 10:15 | 7:30 | 12:15 | *8:15
test: «Ben missed the deadline for his story.» What does missed the deadline mean? | Wrote a story about a missed bus | Read the story out loud | *Handed it in too late | Handed it in early and won a prize
test: «The teacher will extend the deadline to next week.» What does extend the deadline mean? | *Move it to a later time | Forget it completely | Shorten it to today | Hand it in early
exam: Mia starts her poster on Monday so she can finish before the deadline on Thursday. Why does she start early? | To make the deadline shorter | To forget about it | To be late on purpose | *To be sure she finishes in time
